# What Angis cannot do yet

Say, Angis can be taught new wording, but it still has real limits.
Say, It only understands phrases the parser knows, or phrases you define with Define phrase, When I say, or Teach Angis.
Say, It is not a full replacement for Python, C, or JavaScript yet.
Say, Complex low-level systems code, drivers, kernels, compilers, advanced networking, and native apps still need host languages or libraries.
Say, Some features depend on installed Python packages like pygame, OpenGL, databases, or other imports.
Say, The Desktop copy and Apps copy are not the same version.
Say, /Users/fellflow/Apps/Angis is newer and supports more natural Teach Angis flow.
Say, It cannot guess every possible sentence.
Say, If wording is too vague, it needs a phrase definition.
Say, It does not have a mature package ecosystem like npm or pip.
Say, It does not automatically know every API unless you bridge or import it.
Say, Visual apps and games are prototype-level, not production game-engine level.
Say, 3D exists, but not like Unity or Unreal.
Say, Browser and web deployment exist in limited form, not a full React or Next.js style web stack.
Say, Security and permissions are basic.
Say, It is not a hardened sandbox.
Say, Error messages can still be rough when a phrase fails.
Say, Refactoring, autocomplete, type checking, debugging, and IDE tooling are not as mature as mainstream languages.
Say, Some phrase-slot edge cases still need fixes as they are found.
Say, The honest limit is that Angis can be taught almost any wording, but not every capability is native yet.
Say, For deep system work, production web stacks, advanced engines, or unknown APIs, it still needs interpreter work or Python library bridges.
Say, Deep systems work, production web stacks, advanced engines, and unknown APIs still need interpreter work or Python/library bridges.
Say, What Angis does not have yet includes a mature package manager, dependency resolver, lockfile workflow, or public package registry.
Say, It does not have full production web framework features like routing, SSR, hydration, bundling, auth, database migrations, or deployment adapters.
Say, It does not have native mobile app builds for iOS or Android.
Say, It does not have mature desktop app packaging for every operating system.
Say, It does not have advanced game engine systems like physics pipelines, animation graphs, asset importers, shaders, networking replication, or editor tooling.
Say, It does not have a full static type checker, language server, autocomplete engine, formatter, or refactoring engine.
Say, It does not have a hardened permission sandbox, capability isolation, code signing flow, or security audit system.
Say, It does not have built-in cloud infrastructure tools for containers, Kubernetes, serverless, CI/CD, secrets management, or observability.
Say, It does not have native drivers, kernels, embedded firmware support, or real-time systems support.
Say, It does not have complete compatibility with every Python library unless that library is installed and bridged.
Say, It does not have guaranteed production-grade performance for large programs yet.
Say, It does not have complete docs, tutorials, or examples for every feature.
Say, It does not have a formal language specification or standards process yet.
Say, It does not have long-term backwards compatibility guarantees for every phrase and runtime behavior.
Say, It does not have full module versioning, semantic version checks, or compatibility constraints.
Say, It does not have first-class generics, traits, interfaces, macros, decorators, or metaprogramming systems.
Say, It does not have advanced compiler optimizations, bytecode caching policy, incremental compilation, or native code generation.
Say, It does not have full source maps, stack trace mapping, or rich runtime diagnostics for every generated action.
Say, It does not have a complete debugger with watch expressions, breakpoints in every block type, time travel, or memory inspection.
Say, It does not have a profiler, flame graphs, allocation tracking, benchmark runner, or performance regression dashboard.
Say, It does not have a full formatter, linter, unused-code finder, dead-code eliminator, or import organizer.
Say, It does not have project templates, scaffolding commands, migrations, release automation, or changelog tooling.
Say, It does not have workspace management for monorepos, multi-package projects, or plugin dependency graphs.
Say, It does not have official package signing, provenance tracking, software bill of materials, or vulnerability scanning.
Say, It does not have vendoring, offline package mirrors, private package registry support, or reproducible build enforcement.
Say, It does not have full browser DOM APIs, service workers, WebAssembly workflows, PWA support, or browser extension tooling.
Say, It does not have mature CSS layout systems, design token pipelines, accessibility audits, or responsive visual testing.
Say, It does not have full backend framework features like sessions, middleware stacks, ORM migrations, queues, workers, or scheduled jobs.
Say, It does not have production database tooling for schemas, migrations, seed data, connection pools, transactions, backups, or replicas.
Say, It does not have API client generation from OpenAPI, GraphQL schema tooling, gRPC tooling, or contract testing.
Say, It does not have native iOS, Android, watchOS, tvOS, visionOS, or cross-platform mobile UI runtimes.
Say, It does not have app store packaging, signing, notarization, entitlements, provisioning profiles, or release-channel management.
Say, It does not have production desktop installers, auto-update channels, crash reporting, notarization workflow, or enterprise deployment tools.
Say, It does not have full GPU compute, shader language support, render graphs, asset pipelines, or material editors.
Say, It does not have advanced audio engines, MIDI tooling, DAW integration, plugin formats, or low-latency audio guarantees.
Say, It does not have multiplayer matchmaking, authoritative servers, rollback netcode, anti-cheat, or game telemetry systems.
Say, It does not have VR, AR, spatial computing, motion controller, hand tracking, or headset deployment workflows.
Say, It does not have robotics, hardware buses, GPIO, serial device management, CAN bus, or industrial protocol support built in.
Say, It does not have embedded cross-compilation, microcontroller flashing, real-time scheduling, or memory-constrained runtime profiles.
Say, It does not have kernel modules, device drivers, bootloaders, hypervisors, filesystems, or operating-system services built in.
Say, It does not have full networking stacks for TLS management, HTTP/2, HTTP/3, QUIC, DNS, proxies, VPNs, or packet capture.
Say, It does not have distributed systems primitives like consensus, leader election, sharding, replication, or cluster orchestration.
Say, It does not have cloud provider SDK coverage for every service without importing or bridging external libraries.
Say, It does not have infrastructure-as-code planning, drift detection, policy checks, cost estimation, or rollback automation.
Say, It does not have observability pipelines for traces, metrics, logs, alerts, dashboards, SLOs, or incident response.
Say, It does not have enterprise identity systems like SSO, SAML, SCIM, RBAC, audit logs, or tenant isolation built in.
Say, It does not have full cryptography APIs, key management, hardware security module support, or compliance-certified security controls.
Say, It does not have privacy tooling for data retention, deletion requests, consent records, DPIA workflows, or regulatory reports.
Say, It does not have medical, legal, financial, aviation, automotive, or safety-critical certification support.
Say, It does not have advanced AI training, model serving, vector databases, agent orchestration, fine-tuning, or evaluation suites built in.
Say, It does not have notebook-style data science workflows, distributed dataframes, GPU tensors, or experiment tracking natively.
Say, It does not have big-data pipelines for Spark, Flink, Kafka, lakehouses, warehouses, lineage, or data quality checks built in.
Say, It does not have spreadsheet-grade formula engines, pivot tables, workbook rendering, or full Excel compatibility natively.
Say, It does not have full document, PDF, presentation, CAD, GIS, media editing, or publishing pipelines built in.
Say, It does not have localization management, translation memory, pluralization rules, bidi layout testing, or international release workflows.
Say, It does not have collaborative editing, multiplayer cursors, conflict resolution, comments, approvals, or review workflows built in.
Say, It does not have full test frameworks for unit, integration, property, fuzz, mutation, visual, load, chaos, or security testing.
Say, It does not have browser automation, device farms, simulator farms, snapshot baselines, or test flake management built in.
Say, It does not have migration tools to automatically convert large Python, JavaScript, C, Swift, Kotlin, Rust, or Java projects into Angis.
Say, It does not have guaranteed memory safety, thread safety, deterministic concurrency, or race detection for every bridge.
Say, It does not have sandboxed plugin isolation, resource quotas, CPU limits, memory limits, or network egress controls.
Say, It does not have mature accessibility tooling for screen readers, keyboard navigation, contrast checks, or WCAG reporting.
Say, It does not have mature asset management for fonts, images, video, 3D models, licenses, compression, or CDN delivery.
Say, It does not have monetization systems, billing, subscriptions, invoicing, tax handling, refunds, or payment compliance built in.
Say, It does not have marketplace, analytics, growth, notification, messaging, email, SMS, or push infrastructure built in.
Say, It does not have source-control hosting, issue tracking, PR review automation, release gates, or branch protection built in.
Say, It does not have support guarantees, SLAs, governance, formal roadmap, or production incident ownership yet.
Say, It does not have every possible phrase because human language is too open-ended; new wording still needs teaching or parser work.
Say, It does not have every possible capability because Angis is a growing language layer, not a finished universal platform.
Say, Concise missing list: deep systems work, including kernels, drivers, bootloaders, firmware, and real-time systems.
Say, Concise missing list: production web stacks, including full routing, SSR, hydration, bundling, auth, migrations, and deployment adapters.
Say, Concise missing list: advanced engines, including Unity or Unreal level rendering, physics, shaders, asset pipelines, and multiplayer systems.
Say, Concise missing list: mobile builds, including native iOS and Android app packaging and app-store workflows.
Say, Concise missing list: mature package ecosystem, including package registry, dependency resolver, lockfiles, signing, and vulnerability scans.
Say, Concise missing list: full IDE tooling, including language server, autocomplete, formatter, refactoring, rich debugger, and profiler.
Say, Concise missing list: hardened security, including sandboxing, permission isolation, code signing, and audit systems.
Say, Concise missing list: cloud and devops, including Kubernetes, serverless, CI/CD, observability, and infra planning.
Say, Concise missing list: advanced AI and data, including training, serving, vector DBs, big data pipelines, notebooks, and experiment tracking.
Say, Concise missing list: enterprise and regulatory systems, including SSO, RBAC, audit logs, and compliance-certified controls.
Say, Concise missing list: guaranteed production performance, backwards compatibility, and complete documentation.
